# Line endings. The pipeline records a SHA-256 for every published file, and its check command compares
# the files on disk with those hashes. Git for Windows would otherwise convert LF to CRLF on checkout
# and every hash would fail. "-text" tells git never to convert these files. The leading */ makes each
# pattern cover every sport folder.
*/04-data/** -text
*/06-qa/fixtures/** -text
*/02-config/*.csv -text
BLOCKERS.csv -text
# Workbooks are binary: never diff or convert them.
*.xlsx binary
*.xlsm binary
